  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Tuesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A large dome of high pressure continues\nto grip the SW CONUS keeping high temperatures well above normal.\nAfternoon highs 10-15 degrees above normal have prompted an \nExtreme Heat Watch for the region beginning Thursday and lasting \nat least through the weekend. Time outdoors should be limited for \nboth people and animals. Those that work outside should prioritize\nhydration. \n\nSmoke from area wildfires continues to plague the area with\nhampered visibility and low air quality. Those with respiratory \nissues should avoid time outdoors. Smoke is expected to remain in \nthe forecast in the short term under high pressure and light \nwinds.\n\nA slightly tighter pressure gradient in zonal flow just north of\nthe Silver State will increase westerly wind speeds across the\nnorthern border later this week. Afternoon breezes combined with\nvery low RH values and extreme heat will create elevated fire\nweather conditions across northern NV. \n\nFriday and Saturday the positioning of the surface high will\nmeander eastward into the region of the Four Corners. This will \nopen central and southern NV up somewhat to monsoonal flow. \nCurrent guidance has western AZ and the Baja being the main source\nregions for moisture. While PW values aren't spectacular (0.7-0.9\ninches) the threat of convection will return to northern portions\nof Nye and southern White Pine Counties possibly as soon as \nSaturday. Diurnal forcing and sufficient instability make the \nthreat of more dry than wet convection a possibility though \ncurrent probabilities for storm activity remain low. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence continues for\nextreme heat and smoke through the remainder of the week. Moderate\nconfidence exists in elevated fire weather conditions across\nnorthern NV. Low confidence remains in dry storm activity over Nye\nand White Pine Counties this weekend. No major changes needed for\ngrids at this time.",
